# 1️⃣ Java is Simple

## What does Simple mean?

Java was designed to be relatively easy to learn, write, compile, and maintain.

Java removed or simplified several complicated features found in languages such as C++.

### Java does not support:

* Explicit pointer arithmetic
* Operator overloading
* Multiple inheritance through classes
* Manual memory deallocation

### Example

```java
class Student {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int age = 25;

        System.out.println(age);
    }
}
```

The syntax is relatively straightforward.

### 🌍 Real-World Meaning

A beginner can gradually learn Java:

```text
Variables
   ↓
Conditions
   ↓
Loops
   ↓
Methods
   ↓
Classes
   ↓
Objects
```

### 🎯 Interview Point

> Java is considered simple because its syntax is relatively easy to learn and it eliminates several complex features such as pointers and explicit memory management.

