# 5️⃣ Java is Multithreaded

## What is a Thread?

A **thread is a lightweight unit of execution within a program.**

Java allows multiple threads to execute concurrently.

### 🛒 Real-World Example

Imagine an online shopping application:

```text
Shopping Application
        │
        ├── Thread 1 → User Request
        │
        ├── Thread 2 → Payment Processing
        │
        ├── Thread 3 → Inventory Update
        │
        └── Thread 4 → Email Notification
```

These activities can be handled concurrently.

---

## 💻 Simple Java Example

```java
class MyTask extends Thread {

    public void run() {

        System.out.println("Task is running");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        MyTask t = new MyTask();

        t.start();
    }
}
```

### Important

```java
t.start();
```

starts a new thread.

### 🎯 Interview Point

> Java supports multithreading through built-in thread APIs and concurrency utilities, allowing multiple tasks to execute concurrently.

