# 7️⃣ Java is Dynamic

## What does Dynamic mean?

Java supports **dynamic loading and linking of classes at runtime.**

The JVM can load classes when they are needed.

### Basic Flow

```text
Application Starts
       ↓
Required Class Needed
       ↓
Class Loader
       ↓
Loads Class
       ↓
JVM Executes It
```

Java's **Class Loader subsystem** plays an important role here.

### Example

When an application uses a class:

```java
Student student = new Student();
```

The Java class-loading mechanism ensures the required class definition is available for execution.

Java also supports:

* Runtime linking
* Reflection
* Other runtime mechanisms

### 🎯 Interview Point

> Java is dynamic because classes can be loaded and linked at runtime, and Java provides reflection and other runtime mechanisms.

